  "context": "## From Frontier Engineering to Ecosystem Awareness — Twenty Years of Architectural Continuity\nGEPLAN, airport transformation, xSeil and Phylons belong to different operating worlds. Their common thread is a practical architectural problem: a decision depends on information, resources, relationships and assumptions that can change while the system is running. Twenty years of work across those environments gave that problem concrete form. Current research makes its recurring structure explicit and reusable.\n\nHistorical projects supply engineering evidence. Research develops models and interfaces from that experience; pre-standardization work exposes those proposals to wider technical discussion.\nTags: Cartography and ecosystem signals 22.73%; Evidence, provenance and attribution 22.73%; Mobility and infrastructure 22.72%; Transformation and operational continuity 31.82%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/from-frontier-engineering-to-ecosystem-awareness-twenty-years-of-architectural-n2086/\nSource document: https://jubap.net/frontier-engineering-ecosystem-awareness-architectural-continuity/\n\n",
